      "heading": "Abdul Salam vs State Of U.P. on 26 May, 2023",
      "level": 2,
      "content": []
    },
    {
      "heading": "Author: Rajeev Misra",
      "level": 3,
      "content": []
    },
    {
      "heading": "Bench: Rajeev Misra",
      "level": 3,
      "content": [
        "Heard Mr. Saroj Kumar Yadav, the learned counsel for applicant, the learned A.G.A. for State.",
        "This application for bail has been filed by applicant Abdul Salam seeking his enlargement on bail in Case Crime No. 0215 of 2023, under Sections 420 , 120B IPC read with Sections 8 / 13 of Prevention of Corruption Act, 1988, Police Station Khalilabad (Kotwali), District Sant Kabir Nagar, during the pendency of trial.",
        "Perused the record.",
        "Record shows that an F.I.R. dated 07.03.2023 was lodged by first informant, Anshuman Mishra and was registered as Case Crime No.215 of 2023, under Sections 419 , 420 , 120B I.P.C., Sections 66 , 66C of I.T. Act, Section 29 Police Act, 1861 and Sections 7 , 8 & 13 of Prevention of Corruption Act, 1988. In the aforesaid F.I.R. three persons, namely, Sub-Inspector, Kameshwar Mishra, Manoj Kumar Patel and applicant-Virendra Yadav have been nominated as named accused.",
        "Learned counsel for applicant contends that applicant is innocent. Appicant is not named in the F.I.R. Applicant is not a Government Servant either. As such, the provisions of Prevention of Corruption Act cannot apply against applicant.",
        "It is next contended that there are three named accused in the F.I.R. The bail application of named accused Virendra was allowed by this Court, vide order dated 25.4.2023 passed in Criminal Misc. Bail Application No. 18236 of 2023 ( Virendra Vs. State of U.P. ). For ready reference, the same is reproduced herein under:-",
        "10. However, it is made clear that any willful violation of above conditions by the applicant, shall have serious repercussion on his bail so granted by this court and the trial court is at liberty to cancel the bail, after recording the reasons for doing so, in the given case of any of the condition mentioned above.\"",
        "It is next contended that the bail application of named accused H.C. Manoj Kumar Patel was rejected by this Court, vide order dated 9.5.2023 passed in Criminal Misc. Bail Application No. 19675 of 2023. For ready reference, the same is reproduced herein under:-",
        "The case of the present applicant is different from the three named accused. As such, applicant is liable to be enlarged on bail. In case, applicant is enlarged on bail, he shall not misuse the liberty of bail and shall co-operate with the trial.",
        "Per contra, the learned A.G.A. has opposed this application for bail. He submits that since applicant is charge sheeted accused, therefore, he does not deserve any indulgence by this Court. However, the learned A.G.A. could not dislodge the factual/legal submissions urged by the learned counsel for applicant. It is further contended by the learned A.G.A. that the charge sheet has been submitted against applicant on 1.5.2023.",
        "Having heard the learned counsel for applicant, the learned A.G.A. for state, upon perusal of material on record, nature of offence, evidence, complicity of the accused, accusation made and coupled with the fact that applicant is not named in the F.I.R., the applicant not being as Government Servant, therefore, the provisions of Prevention of Corruption Act are not applicable to him, the charge sheet having been submitted, therefore, the evidence sought to be relied upon by the prosecution now stands crystallised, no such circumstance has been pointed out by the learned A.G.A. on the basis of which it can be concluded that custodial arrest of applicant is absolutely necessary during the course of trial, but without making any comment on merits of the case, the applicant has made out a case for bail. Accordingly, the bail application is allowed.",
        "Let the applicant Abdul Salam involved in aforesaid case crime number, be released on bail on his furnishing a personal bond with two sureties each in the like amount to the satisfaction of the court concerned with the following conditions which are being imposed in the interest of justice :-",
        "However, it is made clear that any wilful violation of above conditions by the applicant, shall have serious repercussion on his bail so granted by this court and the trial court is at liberty to cancel the bail, after recording the reasons for doing so, in the given case of any of the condition mentioned above.",
        "Order Date :- 26.5.2023 HSM"
      ]
    },
